					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-622442#post-1706389</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-622442/the-executions-of-doctor-bright#post-1706389</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 09 Feb 2013 04:10:26 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Eric Adler</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>612362</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I guess I can't quite het into bright's Head, er amulet, whtever. I understand the depression over losing Lopez, but why would he destroy her body like that? If he wanted to go back into a chimp, all he'd have to do is transfer the amulet, and then Lopez's body could be put on life support as a 'spare,' or interred with respect.</p> <p>He cannot be killed for good, although he wishes for the peace of the grave, but pain still hurts nonetheless. He's the lonliest man in the universe, with nothing ahead of him but more lonely years and eons and epochs. He will be alive after humanity has passed beyond the veil. After the last biological lifeform in the universe perishes, he will still live on, trapped inside that amulet until the universe ends. Perhaps he'll continue on into the dimensionless oblivion after time itself has withered into nothing. With all that ahead of him, why would he be so willing to add more pain and another death to his memory so soon?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
